  /* 7b strips: [id, title, source, moment keys, note]; keys as in Plate 7, plus pk preliminary, up access, an conformity,
     go change-of-lineage, ap absorption, mg path, ph fruition, x cessation, cu death, ps rebirth-linking. */
  D.sheet7b = {"strips": [["mind-door-following", "The mind-door processes that follow a five-door process (tadanuvattika manodvāra-vīthi)", "the first consequent process: CMA IV guide; the series: later teachers (Ledi Sayadaw; Sayadaw Nandamālābhivaṃsa's Vīthi chart), NOT in the Saṅgaha", "bh bu ma ja ja ja ja ja ja ja ta ta", "the same visible form, just past"], ["mind-door-clear", "Independent mind-door process, limited javana, clear object", "CMA IV §§12–13", "bh bu ma ja ja ja ja ja ja ja ta ta", "any object: past, present, future or timeless; for example, remembering the mango tomorrow"], ["mind-door-obscure", "Independent mind-door process, obscure object", "CMA IV §12", "bh bu ma ja ja ja ja ja ja ja", "no registration"], ["absorption-slow", "Absorption process, first attainment of jhāna, slow faculties", "CMA IV §§14–16", "bh bu ma pk up an go ap b", "Absorption is the 5th javana. The four preceding javanas are one of the four great wholesome cittas with knowledge (great functional with knowledge, 47 48 51 52, for an arahant); joyful before jhānas 1–4, equanimous before the 5th jhāna and the immaterial. At the first attainment absorption occurs once; in a later attainment it can run for as long as resolved."], ["absorption-keen", "Absorption process, keen faculties", "CMA IV §14", "bh bu ma up an go ap b", "The preliminary moment is omitted, so absorption is the 4th javana."], ["path-slow", "Path process (stream-entry), slow faculties", "CMA IV §14; IX (purification by knowledge and vision)", "bh bu ma pk up an go mg ph ph b", "Seven javanas: four preparatory, one path, two fruition. Change-of-lineage is the first citta to take Nibbāna as object, but it cannot cut defilements; the path does. Reviewing processes follow."], ["path-keen", "Path process, keen faculties", "CMA IV §14", "bh bu ma up an go mg ph ph ph b", "No preliminary moment, so three fruition moments follow the path: still seven javanas in all. (Round 1 had this reversed; corrected.)"], ["cessation", "Attainment of cessation (nirodha-samāpatti)", "CMA IV §22; IX", "ap ap x ph b", "Only non-returners and arahants who have all eight attainments, and not in the immaterial planes: cessation needs the eight attainments in succession, and the fine-material jhānas cannot arise there (Vism XXIII). The preparatory moments are not shown."], ["death", "Death and rebirth (reference: Plate 10)", "CMA IV §21; V §§34–41", "ma ja ja ja ja ja ta cu ps b", "Near death javanas run only five times, because the process is weak. Death can follow javana, registration or a life-continuum moment."]], "series": [["taking the past object", "the mind door takes up the colour that the eye-door process has just seen, now past"], ["taking the whole", "the colours of many successive processes are taken together as one"], ["taking the meaning or shape", "the thing is recognised: something round and yellow, a fruit"], ["taking the name", "the name is known: “a mango” (a concept of name). From step 3 on, the object is a concept; liking “the mango” takes a concept as object"]], "seriesNote": "After the eye-door process, at least three mind-door processes follow, according to later teachers: one takes the just-past colour, then the form or whole, then the meaning, and then (for a known thing) the name.", "teaching": "The five-door process knows only the visible datum. 'A mango' is known in later mind-door processes, after the eye-door process is over. So the Plate 7 simile's 'he decides: a ripe mango' at determining should not be read as recognition.", "javana": [["sense-sphere (limited) javana, normal", "7 (sometimes 6)"], ["weak process (e.g. fainting) and at the time of death", "5"], ["the Buddha's Twin Miracle and similar very rapid processes", "4 or 5"], ["first attainment of a jhāna", "absorption 1"], ["direct knowledge (abhiññā)", "1"], ["path", "1"], ["fruition right after the path", "2 (slow) or 3 (keen)"], ["jhāna attainment and fruition attainment", "many, as long as resolved"], ["before cessation", "the 4th immaterial javana 2"], ["emerging from cessation", "fruition 1"]], "registration": ["Registration occurs only after sense-sphere javanas, only in sense-sphere beings, and only with sense-sphere objects that are very great (five doors) or clear (mind door).", "Registration runs for two moments (some commentators allow one), or not at all.", "Feeling: joyful javanas are followed by joyful registration, equanimous by equanimous. With an extremely desirable object, investigating and registration are joyful.", "Desirability is fixed by the object's own nature, not by the person's temperament; the javana's feeling can still vary with the person.", "After javanas with displeasure, registration and life-continuum are equanimous. If the person's life-continuum is joyful, an 'adventitious life-continuum' (āgantuka-bhavaṅga), an investigating citta with equanimity, stands in.", "Registration can follow an arahant's sense-sphere functional javanas; it never follows sublime or supramundane javanas, and never occurs in Brahmā beings."], "attention": ["Whether the javanas are wholesome or unwholesome turns on wise or unwise attention at the turning point of determining.", "In an arahant the javanas are functional (smile-producing or great functional) whatever the attention: no kamma is made."], "byPlane": [80, 64, 42], "byPerson": [54, 56, 44], "notes": ["fine-material plane: no hate-rooted cittas, no nose/tongue/body consciousness, no great resultants (no registration), no sublime resultants in process", "immaterial plane: no five-door cittas at all, no smile, no hate, no great resultants, no fine-material cittas, no path of stream-entry", "stream-enterers and once-returners lack the 4 wrong-view cittas and doubt; non-returners also lack the 2 hate-rooted; arahants have only functional javanas and the arahant fruit"]};
